abstract: >-
  EpiLog is a free, open-source, offline-capable digital field diary for
  epidemiologists and public health workers in low-resource settings.
  Module 2 of the EpiCalc Suite, it provides a structured 4-step field
  diary (basic info, index case, contacts, epidemiological
  characteristics) with automatic calculation of attack rate, case
  fatality rate, and secondary attack rate; an outbreak dashboard with
  epidemic curve and transmission route visualization; CSV/JSON export;
  and one-tap integration with EpiCalc for SIR/SEIR simulation. All data
  is stored locally on-device via IndexedDB, with zero server
  transmission. The app runs entirely offline after first install as a
  Progressive Web App, optimized for 2G/3G network environments.
